# THE FIRST FRAME AFTER A SHAFT'S CROSSING (S5e): the view builds only the chunk
# underfoot on the press (20_realms.ARRIVE_CHUNKS) and streams the ring round it
# in behind, so this is the frame that would show void at its edge if anything
# could. Each shot is the first frame after the crossing's page lifts (an
# `await realm:` waits for the page). Nothing black or empty may be
# in view (S5's bar: never a blank screen). Run from above and over the
# shoulder:
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/arrival.tour --seed=1 --hour=10
#   tools/tour.sh tours/arrival.tour --seed=1 --hour=10 --view=shoulder
#
# 01 down, the first frame under the world. 02 back up, the first frame above.
hour 10
place shaft
await portal 15
press use
await realm:underground 150
shot 01-down-the-first-frame with realm:underground
# Past the settle (20_realms.SETTLE), so the climb is a press of its own.
place shaft
wait 0.6
await portal 15
wait 0.6
press use
await realm:surface 40
shot 02-up-the-first-frame with realm:surface
